From 86fa02e2909ee749ac048a4da689132685435ec9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:20:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: daily scan limits per user, managed from the website

An admin can limit how many cards each user may have read by the vision model (Gemini, or an OpenAI-compatible service such
as Groq) per day: a default for everyone, a limit of their own for a user, or unlimited (an admin can be unlimited too).

The limit is enforced by the server, right before the model is asked, so the website, the CardPulse app and any other client
are held to it. One scan is one photo whose recognition starts. Opening the scanner, a photo that is turned away before it is
read (not an image, too big, no API key, a scanner that has to be tested again), matching, the second opinion from Gemini and
the queue's own retries are not counted; a photo that is read again with Retry is. Photos read together count one scan each,
and a group that no longer fits is read photo by photo instead. The count is one conditional UPDATE, so concurrent requests
cannot pass the limit, and a queued photo carries a marker so the queue's retries never count it twice.

The day is the server's local date: usage starts again at the server's local midnight (in Docker, UTC unless TZ is set), is
stored in the database and survives restarts. A user with no scans left gets HTTP 429 with the daily limit, scans used, scans
remaining and the reset time (and Retry-After); the 429 carries a code that tells it from the rate limiter's. Queueing photos
and Retry are refused up front; photos already queued that no longer fit are marked failed, not retried by themselves.

The time zone this server is meant to run in is America/Detroit (Michigan), set with TZ=America/Detroit for the backend: the
docs and the website's hint use it as the example, and tests cover Michigan's midnight (the 429 and the admin's card name it),
00:00 UTC being an ordinary evening there, and both changes of the clocks (the 25-hour day in November, the 23-hour day in March).

GET /api/scan-limits/me (everyone); /settings, /users and PUT /users/{id} (admins only). Settings -> General -> AI / Card
Scanner gets the default limit, an unlimited switch and the server's time zone and next reset; Settings -> Users shows each
user's limit (default, custom or unlimited) and what they have used today, e.g. 34 / 100 today.

Nothing changes until an admin chooses a number: the default is unlimited. Adds three tables (scan_usage,
scan_limit_overrides, scan_item_charges), created on start-up; no existing table changes. Two upstream composite-processor
tests that use a stand-in session now stub the count. Documented in docs/SCAN_LIMITS.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
