index 0000000..3479d4d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/SCAN_LIMITS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+# Daily scan limits
+
+An administrator can limit how many cards each user may have read by the vision model in a day. The limit is kept and
+enforced **on the server**, right before the model is asked, so it holds for every client: the website, the CardPulse app,
+an older app, or a script that calls the API directly. The apps only show it.
+
+Nothing changes until an administrator chooses a number: the default is **unlimited**.
+
+## What counts as a scan
+
+One *scan* is one photo whose card the vision model is asked to read, whichever model reads it (Gemini, or an
+OpenAI-compatible endpoint such as OpenAI or Groq).
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Counted** | A photo at the moment its recognition starts: the first request to the model for it. Once, however the read turns out. |
+| **Counted again** | A photo whose owner asks for it to be read again (**Retry**). That is another request to the model. |
+| **Not counted** | Opening the scanner or the camera. A photo the server turns away before it reads anything: not an image, too big, nobody signed in, no API key set up, a scanner that has to be tested again. Matching a card that was read with the catalogue. The checks the server makes with the model's help afterwards (comparing pictures, the optional second opinion from Gemini). The retries the queue makes by itself when the model or the network fails. A read that is answered from what the queue already saved. |
+
+Photos that are scanned together (a group read as one picture) count one scan per photo. If a group no longer fits into what
+is left of the day, its photos are read one by one instead, so the ones that fit still get read.
+
+A scan that fails *after* the model was asked (the provider was busy, say) still counts once: the request was made. The queue's
+automatic retries of the same photo do not count again.
+
+## Which limit a user has
+
+1. A user's **own setting** wins: a number of their own (0 switches scanning off for that user) or *unlimited*.
+2. A user without one has the **default**: a number, or unlimited.
+
+Admins are limited like everyone else until their own setting says *unlimited*. (Settings → Users.)
+
+## When a day starts
+
+The day is the **server's local date**: usage starts again at the server's local midnight. In Docker the server's time zone is
+the backend container's, which is **UTC unless `TZ` is set**. To get your own midnight, set it for the backend, for example in
+`.env` (this is Michigan time, with daylight saving looked after by itself):
+
+```
+TZ=America/Detroit
+```
+
+and pass it on (`docker-compose.friends.yml` from the CardPulse repository does this for you). Settings → General → AI / Card
+Scanner shows the time zone the server is using and the next reset, so you can check it. If it says UTC, `TZ` did not reach the
+backend container.
+
+Usage is stored in the database, so restarting the backend does not reset it. A new day needs no job to run: it is a new row
+that starts at zero. Days are kept (one small row per user and day).
+
+## When there are no scans left
+
+A request that would start a read gets **HTTP 429**:
+
+```json
+{
+  "detail": "Daily scan limit reached. Scans reset at midnight (America/Detroit).",
+  "code": "scan_limit_reached",
+  "daily_limit": 100,
+  "unlimited": false,
+  "used": 100,
+  "remaining": 0,
+  "resets_at": "2026-10-10T00:00:00-04:00",
+  "resets_in_seconds": 18720,
+  "timezone": "America/Detroit"
+}
+```
+
+with a `Retry-After` header (seconds until the reset). `code` tells it apart from the rate limiter's 429, which is the one
+that is worth retrying in a moment.
+
+* `POST /api/cards/recognize` (read one photo now): refused before the model is asked.
+* `POST /api/cards/recognize/jobs` (queue photos): refused, and nothing is stored, when the user has **no** scan left. A user
+  with some left may queue more photos than that: scans are counted when each photo starts to be read, and the photos that no
+  longer fit are marked **failed** (*"Daily scan limit reached…"*) without any request to the model. They stay on the review
+  list, and **Retry** reads them once there are scans again.
+* `POST /api/cards/recognize/jobs/{job}/items/{item}/retry`: refused when there is no scan left.
+
+## API
+
+Everything is under `/api/scan-limits`. `null` for a limit or for `remaining` means **unlimited**.
+
+| | | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `GET /me` | any signed-in user | Their allowance today: `daily_limit`, `unlimited`, `used`, `remaining`, `resets_at`, `resets_in_seconds`, `timezone`. |
+| `GET /settings` | admin | The default (`default_limit`, `default_unlimited`) and when a day starts over (`timezone`, `utc_offset`, `reset_time`, `next_reset_at`, `seconds_until_reset`). |
+| `PUT /settings` | admin | `{"default_limit": 100, "default_unlimited": false}`. Either field alone is fine. The number is kept while the default is unlimited. |
+| `GET /users` | admin | The same, and `users`: for each user `mode` (`default`, `custom`, `unlimited`), `custom_limit`, the `daily_limit` that applies, `used` and `remaining` today. |
+| `PUT /users/{id}` | admin | `{"mode": "default"}`, `{"mode": "custom", "limit": 50}` or `{"mode": "unlimited"}`. |
+
+The scan endpoints that poll a job (`GET /api/cards/recognize/jobs/{id}`) and queue one (`POST …/jobs`) also carry the user's
+allowance as `scan_limit`, so a client that polls anyway sees the count move without another request.
+
+## On the website
+
+* **Settings → General → AI / card scanner** (admins): *Default daily scan limit*, with a switch for *Unlimited*, and the time
+  zone and the next reset.
+* **Settings → Users** (admins, multi-user mode): for each user *Use default*, *Custom limit* or *Unlimited*, and how much they
+  have used today (for example `34 / 100 today`).
+
+Only admins can change any of it; the API refuses everyone else with `403`.
+
+## Data
+
+Three small tables, created when the server starts. No existing table or row is changed.
+
+| Table | Holds |
+| --- | --- |
+| `scan_usage` | scans used, per user and day |
+| `scan_limit_overrides` | a user's own setting (none for users on the default) |
+| `scan_item_charges` | which queued photos were already counted, so the queue's retries do not count twice |
+
+The default limit is kept with the other global settings (`settings`: `scan_limit_default` and `scan_limit_default_unlimited`).
